 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Fine-tuning Qwen-1.5-1.8B-Chat with Hugging Face AutoTrain\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook guides you through fine-tuning the `Qwen/Qwen1.5-1.8B-Chat` model using Hugging Face AutoTrain on Google Colab.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps:**\n",
    "1. Setup Colab Environment (GPU, Libraries)\n",
    "2. Mount Google Drive & Prepare Data Path\n",
    "3. Authenticate with Hugging Face\n",
    "4. Prepare Data for AutoTrain (Convert Parquet to CSV/JSONL if needed, ensure correct columns)\n",
    "5. Run AutoTrain Command\n",
    "6. (Optional) Test the fine-tuned model"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup Colab Environment\n",
    "\n",
    "First, ensure you are using a GPU runtime:\n",
    "* Go to `Runtime` -> `Change runtime type`\n",
    "* Select `GPU` (T4 is usually available for free) and click `Save`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install AutoTrain Advanced and other necessary libraries\n",
    "!pip install -U autotrain-advanced pandas pyarrow -q"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Mount Google Drive & Prepare Data Path\n",
    "\n",
    "Mount your Google Drive to access the `finetune_data.parquet` file you uploaded."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount('/content/drive')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --- IMPORTANT: Define the path to your Parquet file --- \n",
    "# Adjust this path based on where you saved the file in your Google Drive\n",
    "google_drive_base_path = '/content/drive/MyDrive/' # Or '/content/drive/MyDrive/YourFolder/'\n",
    "parquet_filename = 'finetune_data.parquet'\n",
    "input_parquet_path = google_drive_base_path + parquet_filename\n",
    "\n",
    "# AutoTrain often works best with data in a local directory within Colab's temporary storage.\n",
    "# We'll copy the data there and potentially convert it if needed.\n",
    "autotrain_data_dir = '/content/autotrain_data'\n",
    "!mkdir -p {autotrain_data_dir}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define the path for the data file within the AutoTrain directory\n",
    "prepared_data_path = f'{autotrain_data_dir}/train.csv' # AutoTrain prefers CSV or JSONL"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Authenticate with Hugging Face\n",
    "\n",
    "You need to log in to Hugging Face to save your fine-tuned model (adapter) to the Hub. You'll need a Hugging Face account and a `WRITE` access token.\n",
    "\n",
    "Get your token here: [https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens](https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from huggingface_hub import notebook_login\n",
    "\n",
    "notebook_login()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Prepare Data for AutoTrain\n",
    "\n",
    "AutoTrain for LLM fine-tuning typically expects a dataset with a specific structure, often a single 'text' column containing the full formatted prompt (instruction + input + output). We need to convert our Parquet data (`instruction`, `input`, `output` columns) into this format.\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll:\n",
    "1. Load the Parquet file using pandas.\n",
    "2. Create a 'text' column formatted appropriately for instruction tuning (e.g., using ChatML format, which Qwen uses).\n",
    "3. Save the result as a CSV file in the `autotrain_data_dir`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load the Parquet data\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    df = pd.read_parquet(input_parquet_path)\n",
    "    print(f\"Loaded {len(df)} records from {input_parquet_path}\")\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Error loading Parquet file: {e}\\nCheck the 'input_parquet_path' variable.\")\n",
    "    # Stop execution if loading fails\n",
    "    raise e \n",
    "\n",
    "# Define the formatting function (using ChatML format for Qwen)\n",
    "def format_chatml(row):\n",
    "    instruction = row['instruction']\n",
    "    input_data = row['input']\n",
    "    output_data = row['output']\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Combine instruction and input based on the task type\n",
    "    # (This logic might need refinement based on how 'input' is structured for different tasks)\n",
    "    if \"RTL 代码片段\" in instruction: # Graph Analysis\n",
    "         user_content = f\"{instruction}\\n\\nInput Code:\\n```\\n{input_data}\\n```\"\n",
    "    elif \"判断代码中存在的保护类型\" in instruction: # Protection Determination\n",
    "         user_content = f\"{instruction}\\n\\nInput Graph JSON:\\n```json\\n{input_data}\\n```\"\n",
    "    elif \"验证代码是否符合规则\" in instruction: # Rule Verification\n",
    "         user_content = f\"{instruction}\\n\\nInput Data JSON:\\n```json\\n{input_data}\\n```\"\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "         user_content = f\"{instruction}\\n\\nInput:\\n{input_data}\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Format as ChatML messages\n",
    "    messages = [\n",
    "        {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are a helpful assistant specialized in RTL code analysis and security verification.\"}, # Optional system prompt\n",
    "        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": user_content},\n",
    "        {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": output_data} # The expected output\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Convert messages to the text format AutoTrain expects (often needs a specific tokenizer application, but we'll try a simple join)\n",
    "    # A better approach might involve using the actual tokenizer, but let's start simple.\n",
    "    # AutoTrain might also handle lists of dictionaries directly depending on the version/setup.\n",
    "    # We will create a single 'text' column assuming AutoTrain can parse it or we format simply.\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Simple text representation (adjust if AutoTrain requires strict ChatML string)\n",
    "    text = f\"<|im_start|>system\\n{messages[0]['content']}<|im_end|>\\n<|im_start|>user\\n{messages[1]['content']}<|im_end|>\\n<|im_start|>assistant\\n{messages[2]['content']}<|im_end|>\"\n",
    "    return text\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply the formatting\n",
    "if 'df' in locals():\n",
    "    df['text'] = df.apply(format_chatml, axis=1)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Keep only the 'text' column needed by AutoTrain\n",
    "    df_autotrain = df[['text']]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Save as CSV\n",
    "    df_autotrain.to_csv(prepared_data_path, index=False)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"Prepared data saved to {prepared_data_path}\")\n",
    "    print(\"\\nExample formatted text:\")\n",
    "    print(df_autotrain['text'].iloc[0])\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"DataFrame 'df' not loaded. Cannot prepare data.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Run AutoTrain Command\n",
    "\n",
    "Now we configure and run the `autotrain llm` command.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Parameters:**\n",
    "*   `--train`: Flag to indicate training.\n",
    "*   `--model`: The base model ID from Hugging Face Hub (`Qwen/Qwen1.5-1.8B-Chat`).\n",
    "*   `--project-name`: A name for your AutoTrain project (will also be the repo name on the Hub).\n",
    "*   `--data-path`: Path to the directory containing your prepared training data (`autotrain_data_dir`). AutoTrain expects `train.csv` or `train.jsonl` inside.\n",
    "*   `--text-column`: The name of the column containing the formatted text data (`text`).\n",
    "*   `--use-peft`: Use Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning (PEFT), specifically LoRA.\n",
    "*   `--quantization`: Use quantization (e.g., `int4`) to reduce memory usage.\n",
    "*   `--lr`: Learning rate.\n",
    "*   `--batch-size`: Training batch size (adjust based on Colab GPU memory).\n",
    "*   `--epochs`: Number of training epochs.\n",
    "*   `--trainer`: Specify the trainer type (e.g., `sft` for supervised fine-tuning).\n",
    "*   `--push-to-hub`: Push the resulting adapter model to the Hub.\n",
    "*   `--token`: Your Hugging Face token (if not picked up from login automatically).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Note:** You might need to adjust `--batch-size`, `--gradient-accumulation`, `--block-size` (sequence length), and `--lr` based on your specific dataset and Colab's GPU memory limits (T4 GPU)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --- AutoTrain Configuration ---\n",
    "# Make sure to replace 'YourHuggingFaceUsername' with your actual username\n",
    "hf_username = \"YourHuggingFaceUsername\" \n",
    "project_name = \"qwen1.5-1.8b-cfe-racfe-finetune\" # Choose a project name\n",
    "base_model = \"Qwen/Qwen1.5-1.8B-Chat\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Adjust parameters based on Colab T4 memory and your data\n",
    "# Small batch size is crucial for Colab free tier\n",
    "batch_size = 1 \n",
    "gradient_accumulation = 8 # Effective batch size = batch_size * gradient_accumulation\n",
    "epochs = 1 # Start with 1 epoch\n",
    "learning_rate = 2e-4\n",
    "block_size = 1024 # Max sequence length (adjust based on data and memory)\n",
    "lora_r = 16\n",
    "lora_alpha = 32\n",
    "\n",
    "# Construct the AutoTrain command\n",
    "# Using ! allows running shell commands in Colab\n",
    "autotrain_command = f\"\"\"\n",
    "autotrain llm \\n\
    --train \\n\
    --model {base_model} \\n\
    --project-name {project_name} \\n\
    --data-path {autotrain_data_dir} \\n\
    --text-column text \\n\
    --lr {learning_rate} \\n\
    --batch-size {batch_size} \\n\
    --epochs {epochs} \\n\
    --gradient-accumulation {gradient_accumulation} \\n\
    --block-size {block_size} \\n\
    --quantization int4 \\n\
    --use-peft \\n\
    --lora-r {lora_r} \\n\
    --lora-alpha {lora_alpha} \\n\
    --lora-dropout 0.05 \\n\
    --logging-steps 10 \\n\
    --eval-strategy none \\n\
    --save-total-limit 1 \\n\
    --save-strategy steps \\n\
    --save-steps 50 \\n\
    --disable-tqdm True \\n\
    --push-to-hub \\n\
    --repo-id {hf_username}/{project_name} \n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "# Note: We removed --token flag, assuming notebook_login() worked.\n",
    "# If push fails, you might need to add: --token $(cat ~/.huggingface/token)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"--- AutoTrain Command ---\")\n",
    "print(autotrain_command)\n",
    "print(\"--- Starting Training ---\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Execute the command\n",
    "!{autotrain_command}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
